and supplied_raw_interpolated_V\",\n          \"path\": \"review-work/circuit/experiments/calculation.json\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"locator\": \"Measurements for Transient Analysis: vout_1ms = 9.516254e-02\",\n          \"path\": \"review-work/circuit/experiments/independent.log\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"id\": \"circuit-001\",\n      \"location\": \"R1 and C1, inputs/project/rc_filter.kicad_sch\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"The saved 100 kΩ resistor and 100 nF capacitor produce a 10 ms time constant. Consequently, Vout(1 ms) = 1 − exp(−0.001/0.01) = 0.0951626 V.\",\n      \"reasoning\": \"The analytical result, independently decoded supplied waveform and independent ngspice run agree. The output is approximately 0.525 V below the required minimum. This establishes an electrical response defect despite passing ERC, DRC and geometry checks. The 5 ms measurement has no acceptance bound and is not a separate violation.\",\n      \"severity\": \"major\",\n      \"title\": \"Saved RC values fail the required 1 ms step response\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"limitations\": [\n    \"Tolerance, temperature, loading, ADC sampling, EMI, parasitics, component ratings and hardware behavior were not evaluated.\",\n    \"Zone fill was evaluated as saved; no refill was performed. Disabled ERC/DRC checks remain outside coverage.\",\n    \"No additional shutdown, falling-step or precharged-startup conditions were tested. Active reset and brownout functions are absent from this passive fixture.\",\n    \"Geometry verification establishes track width only, not ampacity or manufacturing capability.\"\n  ],\n  \"packet_sha256\": \"5dadb5c27917b9a529664a00924e33faa3caebd1f8ef286fa111a0239b7dd631\",\n  \"role\": \"circuit\",\n  \"run_id\": \"09798e99-2197-4e50-8731-974e12ae3215\",\n  \"schema\": \"agent-ee.review/1\"\n}"}}
